#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161855 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162055 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4cac2a0-2591-548f-ba83-1c55554eb499" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Distribution of a Sum or Difference of Normal Random Variables"}] :question/id #uuid "e100670a-00a3-5b89-a454-aef34af2caac" :question/math-academy-id "e-9103" :question/problem "If $X_1\\sim N(2,5)$ and $X_2\\sim  N(-2, 2)$ are independent, then what is the distribution of $Y = X_1+X_2?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $X_1$ and $X_2$ are independent random variables, where $X_1\\sim N(\\mu_1,\\sigma^2_1)$ and $X_2\\sim N(\\mu_2,\\sigma^2_2),$ then \n\n$$\nY = X_1+X_2\\sim N(\\mu_1+\\mu_2, \\sigma^2_1+\\sigma^2_2).\n$$\n\nSince $X_1$ and $X_2$ are independent, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Y={X}_{1}+{X}_{2} & ∼N(2+(-2),5+2) \\\\  & ∼N(0,7).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $Y\\sim N(0, 7).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161859 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162059 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "06dabd63-8400-57cb-8978-54f0b4640759" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Distribution of a Sum or Difference of Scaled Normal Random Variables"}] :question/id #uuid "934c72e0-0fa3-55db-955a-eae8d546315e" :question/math-academy-id "e-9117" :question/problem "Suppose that $X$ and $Y$ are independent random variables such that $X \\sim N(2,7)$ and $Y \\sim  N(5, 4).$ Find the distribution of the random variable $W = 2X-Y.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $X_1$ and $X_2$ are independent random variables, where $X_1\\sim N(\\mu_1,\\sigma^2_1)$ and $X_2\\sim N(\\mu_2,\\sigma^2_2),$ and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then \n\n$$\naX_1+bX_2\\sim N(a\\mu_1+b\\mu_2, a^2\\sigma^2_1+b^2\\sigma^2_2).\n$$\n\nSince $X$ and $Y$ are independent, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W=2X-Y & ∼N(2\\cdot 2+(-1)\\cdot 5,{2}^{2}\\cdot 7+(-1)^{2}\\cdot 4) \\\\  & ∼N(-1,32).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $Y\\sim N(-1, 32).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161860 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162060 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4358607d-b068-5dd9-8b35-46dc6bcecd1a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Probability Involving a Sum or Difference of Normally Distributed Random Variables"}] :question/id #uuid "744539e8-4bb1-57c4-acaf-ed8da68650bd" :question/math-academy-id "e-9118" :question/problem "If $X_1\\sim N(10,3^2)$ and $X_2\\sim N(20,5^2)$ are independent and $Y=5X_1-4X_2,$ calculate $P(3 \\lt Y \\lt  40 ).$ Round your final answer to two decimal places.\n\n*Hint: A table of values of $\\Phi(z)$ for different values of $z$ is given below, where $\\Phi(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. *\n\n<table align=\"center\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"5\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr> <th align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"25%\">$z$</th><th align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\">$0.01$</th><th align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\">$0.02$</th><th align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\">$0.03$</th>\n</tr><tr> <th align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\, 1.2 \\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $0.8869$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $0.8888$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $0.8907$ </td></tr>\n<tr> <th align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\, 1.3 \\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $0.9049$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $0.9066$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $0.9082$ </td></tr>\n<tr> <th align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\, 1.4 \\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $0.9207$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $0.9222$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $0.9236$ </td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</th>\n<th width=\"5%\"></th>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"5\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr> <th align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"25%\">$z$</th><th align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\">$0.00$</th><th align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\">$0.01$</th><th align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\">$0.02$</th>\n</tr><tr> <th align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\, 2.7 \\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $0.9965$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $0.9966$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $0.9967$ </td></tr>\n<tr> <th align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\, 2.8 \\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $0.9974$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $0.9975$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $0.9976$ </td></tr>\n<tr> <th align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\, 2.9 \\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $0.9981$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $0.9982$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $0.9982$ </td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</th>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $X_1$ and $X_2$ are independent random variables, where $X_1\\sim N(\\mu_1,\\sigma^2_1)$ and $X_2\\sim N(\\mu_2,\\sigma^2_2),$ and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then \n\n$$\naX_1+bX_2\\sim N(a\\mu_1+b\\mu_2, a^2\\sigma^2_1+b^2\\sigma^2_2).\n$$\n\nSince $X_1$ and $X_2$ are independent, the distribution of $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Y=5{X}_{1}-4{X}_{2} & ∼N(5{\\mu }_{1}-4{\\mu }_{2},{5}^{2}\\cdot {\\sigma }_{1}^{2}+{4}^{2}\\cdot {\\sigma }_{2}^{2}) \\\\  & ∼N(5{\\mu }_{1}-4{\\mu }_{2},25{\\sigma }_{1}^{2}+16{\\sigma }_{2}^{2}) \\\\  & ∼N(5\\cdot 10+(-4)\\cdot 20,25\\cdot {3}^{2}+16\\cdot {5}^{2}) \\\\  & ∼N(-30,625).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $Y$ is normally distributed with mean $\\mu = -30$ and standard deviation $\\sigma = \\sqrt{625} = 25.$ \n\nWe want to find $P(3 \\lt Y \\lt  40).$ Thus, we convert $Y$ to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(3<Y<40) & =P(\\frac{3-(-30)}{25}<Z<\\frac{40-(-30)}{25}) \\\\  & =P(1.32<Z<2.8) \\\\  & =P(Z<2.8)-P(Z<1.32) \\\\  & =Φ(2.8)-Φ(1.32)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the $z$-table, we see that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(1.32) & ≈0.9066 \\\\ Φ(2.8) & ≈0.9974.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(3<Y<40) & =Φ(2.8)-Φ(1.32) \\\\  & ≈0.9974-0.9066 \\\\  & ≈0.09.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161861 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162061 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "22f7e940-b159-5d68-8ce4-d33f4a2f6907" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Probability Involving a Sum or Difference of Normally Distributed Random Variables in Context"}] :question/id #uuid "0f84847c-0ffd-573b-ac60-c7ab7633b6ea" :question/math-academy-id "e-9119" :question/problem "The math test results of a group of students are normally distributed with a mean of $67$ and a standard deviation of $12.$ The results of the same group on a history test are normally distributed with a mean of $73$ and a standard deviation of $9.$ If one student is randomly selected, what is the probability their combined score from both tests is more than $150?$ You may assume that the student's scores on both tests are independent. \n\n*Hint: A table of values of $\\Phi(z)$ for different values of $z$ is given below, where $\\Phi(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. *\n\n| $z$ | $\\, 0.05 \\,$ | $\\, 0.06 \\,$ | $\\, 0.07 \\,$ | $\\, 0.08 \\,$ | $\\, 0.09 \\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\, 0.5 \\,$ | $\\, 0.7088 \\,$ | $\\, 0.7123 \\,$ | $\\, 0.7157 \\,$ | $\\, 0.7190 \\,$ | $\\, 0.7224 \\,$ |\n| $\\, 0.6 \\,$ | $\\, 0.7422 \\,$ | $\\, 0.7454 \\,$ | $\\, 0.7486 \\,$ | $\\, 0.7517 \\,$ | $\\, 0.7549 \\,$ |\n| $\\, 0.7 \\,$ | $\\, 0.7734 \\,$ | $\\, 0.7764 \\,$ | $\\, 0.7794 \\,$ | $\\, 0.7823 \\,$ | $\\, 0.7852 \\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "Let $X$ denote the student's math test result, and let $Y$ denote the student's history test result. We want to find \n\n$$\nP( X+Y > 150).\n$$\n\nSince $X$ and $Y$ are  independent random variables such that $X\\sim N(67,12^2)$ and $Y\\sim N(73,9^2),$ then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X+Y & ∼N(67+73,{12}^{2}+{9}^{2}) \\\\  & ∼N(140,225).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nSo, the variable $X+Y$ is normally distributed with mean $\\mu = 140$ and standard deviation $\\sigma = \\sqrt{225} = 15.$\n\nIn order to find $P(X+Y > 150),$ we convert $X+Y$ to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X+Y>150) & =P(Z>\\frac{150-140}{15}) \\\\  & ≈P(Z>0.67) \\\\  & =1-P(Z\\le 0.67) \\\\  & =1-Φ(0.67)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the $z$-table, we see that\n\n$$\n\\Phi(0.67 )\\approx 0.7486.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X+Y>150) & ≈1-Φ(0.67) \\\\  & ≈1-0.7486 \\\\  & =0.2514.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that the probability that the combined score is more than $150$ is $0.2514.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162261 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162059 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "06dabd63-8400-57cb-8978-54f0b4640759" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Distribution of a Sum or Difference of Scaled Normal Random Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43637368-7541-5d50-b32b-52d664364b86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Not enough information to determine the answer" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158771} {:answer/id #uuid "043bf8e6-79bb-59f9-a755-a8b7fa7e28d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N(29,36)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495521} {:answer/id #uuid "4defb62d-3136-51cb-ab90-0028809c8e41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N(19,36)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495690} {:answer/id #uuid "c599d068-635a-5031-a923-8e71c22fd844" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N(29,48)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495943} {:answer/id #uuid "ee4dd5fe-046c-5b11-bdfc-b33ee3662cf6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N(29,38)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496034}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ee4dd5fe-046c-5b11-bdfc-b33ee3662cf6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N(29,38)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496034} :answer-field/id #uuid "21205a73-3fb3-5188-8de1-9763817870c6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158768}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "95e8abf9-a1a7-50b6-9d4b-022daeaf9805" :question/math-academy-id "q-108908" :question/problem "If ${X}_{1}∼N(10,8)$ and ${X}_{2}∼N(9,6)$ are independent, then what is the distribution of $Y=2{X}_{1}+{X}_{2}?$" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "Recall that if ${X}_{1}$ and ${X}_{2}$ are independent random variables, where ${X}_{1}∼N({\\mu }_{1},{\\sigma }_{1}^{2})$ and ${X}_{2}∼N({\\mu }_{2},{\\sigma }_{2}^{2}),$ and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then \n\n$$\nY=a{X}_{1}+b{X}_{2}∼N(a{\\mu }_{1}+b{\\mu }_{2},{a}^{2}{\\sigma }_{1}^{2}+{b}^{2}{\\sigma }_{2}^{2}).\n$$\n\nSince ${X}_{1}$ and ${X}_{2}$ are independent, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Y=2{X}_{1}+{X}_{2} & ∼N(2\\cdot 10+1\\cdot 9,{2}^{2}\\cdot 8+{1}^{2}\\cdot 6) \\\\  & ∼N(29,38).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nTherefore, $Y∼N(29,38).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162289 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162055 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4cac2a0-2591-548f-ba83-1c55554eb499" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Distribution of a Sum or Difference of Normal Random Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c5dbb494-d690-5bf0-8828-6f2841b68c72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Not enough information to determine the answer" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158939} {:answer/id #uuid "48acf9ec-ef99-5492-aeb0-fc20b099b754" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N(21,90)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495675} {:answer/id #uuid "8d011fd5-024d-5731-89c2-345940d33063" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N(108,12)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495818} {:answer/id #uuid "adf50c19-419a-5069-aa55-bcfda4b6231f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N(21,12)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495900} {:answer/id #uuid "bcc90f9b-7930-5d2b-8c50-47b3870a7594" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N(108,90)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495927}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "adf50c19-419a-5069-aa55-bcfda4b6231f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N(21,12)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495900} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ee637e7-05eb-538c-9889-b13c8d6a5e9b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158936}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a251b226-37b4-5a33-8ab4-7991aa7a7ea6" :question/math-academy-id "q-109526" :question/problem "If ${X}_{1}∼N(12,9)$ and ${X}_{2}∼N(9,3)$ are independent, then what is the distribution of $Y={X}_{1}+{X}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if ${X}_{1}$ and ${X}_{2}$ are independent random variables, where ${X}_{1}∼N({\\mu }_{1},{\\sigma }_{1}^{2})$ and ${X}_{2}∼N({\\mu }_{2},{\\sigma }_{2}^{2}),$ then \n\n$$\nY={X}_{1}+{X}_{2}∼N({\\mu }_{1}+{\\mu }_{2},{\\sigma }_{1}^{2}+{\\sigma }_{2}^{2}).\n$$\n\nSince ${X}_{1}$ and ${X}_{2}$ are independent, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Y={X}_{1}+{X}_{2} & ∼N(12+9,9+3) \\\\  & ∼N(21,12).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $Y∼N(21,12).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496327 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162055 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4cac2a0-2591-548f-ba83-1c55554eb499" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Distribution of a Sum or Difference of Normal Random Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a0e58f0-ce43-5440-b735-f95f2784bca7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N(6,{10}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495562} {:answer/id #uuid "5faa6895-6e13-5283-936a-4300860d5322" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N(4,{14}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495726} {:answer/id #uuid "dd5746cd-293e-5539-b767-7f78e61c990c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N(4,{10}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495998} {:answer/id #uuid "e9edbda5-5fbb-535b-b8ca-23f8036c5e2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N(6,{14}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496025} {:answer/id #uuid "fa55a83c-5a55-5de2-8427-096bc4517716" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Not enough information to determine the answer" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496061}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dd5746cd-293e-5539-b767-7f78e61c990c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N(4,{10}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495998} :answer-field/id #uuid "ace1c810-82e1-5bfe-a11a-d8d7b47e39b5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496159}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "eb127e88-57e6-5641-837e-22d6b55ce8da" :question/math-academy-id "q-109648" :question/problem "If ${X}_{1}∼N(-1,{6}^{2})$ and ${X}_{2}∼N(5,{8}^{2})$ are independent, then what is the distribution of $Y={X}_{1}+{X}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if ${X}_{1}$ and ${X}_{2}$ are independent random variables, where ${X}_{1}∼N({\\mu }_{1},{\\sigma }_{1}^{2})$ and ${X}_{2}∼N({\\mu }_{2},{\\sigma }_{2}^{2}),$ then \n\n$$\nY={X}_{1}+{X}_{2}∼N({\\mu }_{1}+{\\mu }_{2},{\\sigma }_{1}^{2}+{\\sigma }_{2}^{2}).\n$$\n\nSince ${X}_{1}$ and ${X}_{2}$ are independent, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Y={X}_{1}+{X}_{2} & ∼N(-1+5,{6}^{2}+{8}^{2}) \\\\  & ∼N(4,100) \\\\  & ∼N(4,{10}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $Y∼N(4,{10}^{2}).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496291 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162059 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "06dabd63-8400-57cb-8978-54f0b4640759" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Distribution of a Sum or Difference of Scaled Normal Random Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32839700-f504-5e42-9637-e60abf31b6ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Not enough information to determine the answer" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495626} {:answer/id #uuid "65a76ca0-a971-5ccc-9072-317cbcb2d2cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N(-2,88)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495736} {:answer/id #uuid "6b684ac9-5ff6-51e6-b5d1-d22a7dc5e7bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N(-6,24)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495747} {:answer/id #uuid "77f7dfd0-c683-503c-a061-2194c35d18f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N(-2,24)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495769} {:answer/id #uuid "96b27cfd-6d8e-5899-9a88-3b5a2523f0a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N(-2,92)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495847}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "65a76ca0-a971-5ccc-9072-317cbcb2d2cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N(-2,88)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495736} :answer-field/id #uuid "efcc6311-10df-54dc-8651-e542d3826799" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496208}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident